WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.340 --> 00:00:06.839
Charter schooling introduced many

00:00:06.839 --> 00:00:08.700
important innovations. It showed how we

00:00:08.700 --> 00:00:10.380
could have school choice inside of

00:00:10.380 --> 00:00:13.019
public education; how nonprofits could

00:00:13.019 --> 00:00:15.059
run public schools; how great public

00:00:15.060 --> 00:00:16.920
schools can be replicated or expanded.

00:00:16.920 --> 00:00:19.650
But we've never made full use of one of

00:00:19.650 --> 00:00:21.080
the charter schooling's most important

00:00:21.090 --> 00:00:22.800
contributions: contract-based

00:00:22.800 --> 00:00:25.140
accountability. A charter school

00:00:25.140 --> 00:00:27.510
negotiates performance contracts with an

00:00:27.510 --> 00:00:29.789
authorizer. That contract lays out

00:00:29.789 --> 00:00:31.349
exactly what the school will accomplish.

00:00:31.349 --> 00:00:34.290
In exchange, the school then gets

00:00:34.290 --> 00:00:36.329
freedom from a wide array of rules.

00:00:36.329 --> 00:00:38.640
Now, if the charter school succeeds, its

00:00:38.640 --> 00:00:40.920
contract will be renewed. But if it fails

00:00:40.920 --> 00:00:43.050
to meet its performance goals, the school

00:00:43.050 --> 00:00:45.440
will be closed and replaced. The new

00:00:45.440 --> 00:00:47.340
federal education law encourages states

00:00:47.340 --> 00:00:49.079
to create accountability systems

00:00:49.079 --> 00:00:49.800
that are new.

00:00:49.800 --> 00:00:51.870
So why not apply contract-based

00:00:51.870 --> 00:00:53.850
accountability to all public schools in

00:00:53.850 --> 00:00:55.800
a city, including those run by the

00:00:55.800 --> 00:00:58.500
traditional school district? This is the

00:00:58.500 --> 00:00:59.969
way for all of the city's schools -

00:00:59.969 --> 00:01:02.879
charter schools and district schools - to

00:01:02.879 --> 00:01:04.920
have equal operational freedom and be

00:01:04.920 --> 00:01:06.800
held equally accountable.

00:01:06.800 --> 00:01:08.840
To learn more about my take on charter school

00:01:08.850 --> 00:01:10.799
accountability, check the links in the

00:01:10.799 --> 00:01:13.140
description below. Also, let us know what

00:01:13.140 --> 00:01:14.939
other topics you want AEI scholars to

00:01:14.939 --> 00:01:18.080
cover in 60 seconds.

